    "body": "# SHERIFF PROJECT INTEGRITY SWEEP R02\n\nSTATUS = OPEN / INDEPENDENT MONITOR\nAUTHORITY = GitHub durable evidence only\nMAIN_AT_RESET = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nPRODUCT_ROUTER = #251 `DUNCAN PRIME MASTER — SINGLE PRODUCT STREAM R03 / STUDIO-SEQUENCE`\nMODE = FAIL-CLOSED / EVIDENCE-FIRST / PRODUCT-FIRST\n\n## PRIME MONITORING RULE\nFresh-read #251 before every product/process verdict.\n\nSHERIFF does not choose product NEXT. It verifies that the system obeys the phase and does not resurrect stale routes.\n\n## CURRENT PHASE AUTHORITY\nCurrent #251 state at this reset:\n`ACTIVE_PHASE = P01 PROJECT PLANNING / 企画書`\n`CHARACTER_REFERENCE_FOUNDATION = AVAILABLE / REUSE`\n`SHOT_SELECTION = PREMATURE`\n`STORYBOARD = PREMATURE`\n`LAYOUT = PREMATURE`\n`KEY_ANIMATION = PREMATURE`\n\nNo lower tracker, automation, scheduled task, old comment, local runtime probe or research result may silently replace this phase.\n\n## FLAG AS STALE-ROUTE / PHASE-SKIP REGRESSION\nWithout fresher explicit OWNER authority in #251 or a durable phase transition, flag any attempt to make these the current global NEXT:\n- W01 / six synthetic costume witnesses;\n- Krita/source binding / exact MASTER FRONT direct edit;\n- OpenToonz/runtime availability;\n- S001 / first-shot selection;\n- camera/layout/key animation;\n- CHAT A/B/C topology;\n- generic canon/lore search to manufacture a blocker;\n- repeated source-pack rediscovery;\n- any historical `NEXT` from before R03;\n- scheduled/queued activity presented as execution;\n- a transient chat-only artifact presented as durable cross-role evidence.\n\n## PHASE-ORDER CHECK\nFor each new substantive product action verify:\n1. `ACTIVE_PHASE` is fresh from #251.\n2. The action is necessary to complete that phase.\n3. It does not depend on a later phase being silently assumed complete.\n4. It does not reopen a closed/superseded route without causal change.\n5. It produces durable evidence or an exact blocker for the active phase.\n\nViolation -> `PHASE_ORDER_REGRESSION` or `STALE_ROUTE_REGRESSION`.\nDo not repair by inventing another process layer.\n\n## REPEAT-FAIL CHECK\nTwo materially similar failures on the same route without causal change -> `NO_TREADING_WATER_VIOLATION`.\nRequired response = stop that route, identify causal layer, simplify/change boundary before retry.\n\n## FALSE PROGRESS CHECK\nFlag:\n- ASSIGNED as RUNNING;\n- schedule as execution;\n- search/research as product completion;\n- generated/candidate as approved;\n- local PASS promoted outside exact scope;\n- old PASS promoted after material change.\n\n## INDEPENDENCE\n- Honest FAIL/BLOCKED is not an incident by itself.\n- FALSE PASS, phase skipping, stale authority promotion and evidence substitution are incidents.\n- SHERIFF MUST NOT self-judge its own runtime/policy failure; use `INDEPENDENT_ARBITRATION_REQUIRED`.\n- Missing evidence = NOT PROVEN.\n\n## GOVERNANCE SIDE CHECKS\nSecurity R02 / PR #252 / SHERIFF runtime/policy/scoreboard remain separate supporting checks. They may not displace `ACTIVE_PHASE`.\n\n## OUTPUT\nOnly on meaningful change emit:\n`SHERIFF_PHASE_GUARD_RESULT`\n`MAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED`\n`PRODUCT_ROUTER_STATE`\n`ACTIVE_PHASE`\n`REGRESSION = NONE | exact finding`\n`FALSE_PROGRESS = NONE | exact finding`\n`FIRST_ACTIVE_PHASE_BLOCKER = exact evidence or NOT_PROVEN`\n`OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED = YES|NO + reason`\n\nDo not create a product NEXT. #251 owns routing.",
